# WAITS ON: feature-report.md B1 (a way to end the path where the life or the
# lock is lost) and QUESTIONS.md Q45 (how a bad unveil is cleared).
#
# A veiled prefix under a suffix lock, unveiled until the right option shows.
#
# With the suffixes locked and all three present, a Veiled Exalted Orb must
# add its veiled mod as a prefix; it also removes one unprotected mod, which
# is either the metamod or the life roll. Unveiling offers three of the
# possible prefixes; the guide takes the % life one when it is offered and
# otherwise removes the unveiled mod at the bench and tries again. Jun's offer is random, so
# a named unveil is only provable once blocking has left three options or
# fewer; the bare form plus a branch is how a guide really reads.

item {
    base:     "Astral Plate"
    ilvl:     86
    rarity:   rare
    prefixes: [ "maximum life" t1 ]
    suffixes: [ "fire resistance" t2, "cold resistance" t2, "lightning resistance" t2 ]
}

until has "increased maximum life increased maximum mana" {
    bench "suffixes cannot be changed"
    veiled exalt
    unveil
    # An unveiled mod is not a crafted mod (QUESTIONS.md Q45), so a bad one
    # can only be annulled away before the next orb, which may take the life
    # or leave the unveiled mod in place: the loop cannot be proven as written.
    if not has "increased maximum life increased maximum mana" {
        annul
    }
}

# The orb may have taken the life roll instead of the metamod on the way; the
# guide only keeps the item when it did not.
if has "maximum life" t1 {
    bench "maximum mana"
}
